{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antiparasitic, Hemolytic, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (61.9%) to Hylin a1. Activity: Active against bacteria and parasites. Inhibits Gram+ E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC 8 uM), S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC 4 uM), S. epidermidis ATCC 12228 (MIC 2 uM), E. casseliflavus ATCC 700327 (MIC 16 uM), Gram- E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 16 uM), K. pneumoniae ATCC 13883 (MIC 4 uM), and parasite T. cruzi (IC50 15.9 uM). It also inhibits cancer cell proliferation (NIH/3T3, B16F10 cells, MCF-7 cells, and HeLa cells, IC50 10-14 uM). Structure: Helical in 50% TFE. In vitro Toxicity: highly hemolytic at 10 uM", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "32967114", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antibiotics (Basel). 2020 Sep 21;9(9):625. doi: 10.3390/antibiotics9090625. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03248", "source_id": "AP03248", "source_numeric_id": "03248", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03248", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Figainin 1, a Novel Amphibian Skin Peptide with Antimicrobial and Antiproliferative Properties", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
